+### Fixture observations of Actor command work
+
+The same default-off `fixture-clock` feature exposes
+`testing::pair_with_capture_clock_and_work(config, session, capacity, clock)`.
+It returns the original single-connection setup future and scripted service,
+plus one `ActorWork` reader. Existing pair, connector and Supervisor factories
+remain unobserved. The recorder is installed after actual setup acknowledgement
+but before InputSender publication and Actor spawn. Dropping an unpolled setup
+future therefore has no installed Actor or invented work receipt.
+
+The reader contains no task, clock, protocol marker or unbounded event history.
+One private allocation identity binds its snapshots; equal SessionIds from two
+fixtures do not make their snapshots interchangeable. One AtomicWaker serves one
+mutable `changed` waiter. Fixed-size counters, one active command, one last return
+receipt and one last completed maintenance receipt are the whole retained state.
+Counters never wrap; overflow, poison and invalid installation latch a fault.
+They do not replace any original result or make a failed observation complete.
+Dropping the reader neither changes admission nor shuts down the connection.
+
+The boundaries are deliberately different:
+
+- `accepted` advances only after the original mpsc `try_send` returns success.
+  `publications_in_flight` covers the publication interval: another thread may
+  handle a command before its sender publishes the accepted count. Rejections
+  count only attempts that reached the enqueue boundary; prior public validation
+  failures remain prior validation failures. Counter publication order is not a
+  per-command queue ticket.
+- `commands_returned` advances only after the actual command body returns its
+  unchanged `Result`. Both the ordinary select branch and the original image
+  queue replay use this common wrapper. A dropped or panicking entered body
+  increments `commands_abandoned`; it never produces a returned-success receipt.
+  An unpolled wrapper has not entered the body. The original after-stop discard
+  branch has its own count and is never a handler return.
+- The last receipt copies only command kind, request/sequence metadata, its real
+  result and fixed-size buffer facts. An Audio result can be Ok while its samples
+  are deliberately kept behind an earlier response. That is handling, not a
+  socket send. There is no PCM, text, image or tool payload in this recorder.
+- `last_maintenance` is published only after the entire original maintenance
+  pass reaches the next select, including any awaited writes. Its covered
+  returned-command and post-stop-discard counts are captured together at pass
+  entry, before the first maintenance operation. Commands replayed late inside
+  an image write have not had that whole pass after their return; only a later
+  completed pass can cover them. Buffer facts instead describe pass completion.
+  A canceled pass or a pass that exits early on an original error is incomplete.
+  Commands removed from mpsc into an image write's private queue are still
+  unhandled; a failed image write may drop them without entering the common
+  handler.
+
+These are historical facts, not an idle state. No receipt proves that a select
+branch was polled, a due tick handled, a socket flushed, a remote frame handled,
+an output consumed, or a task joined. The unchanged select fairness, ticker,
+explicit frame yield, capture-age checks and deadlines remain in place. There
+is no method granting clock advancement. Even matching accepted/returned counts
+need a separately frozen producer frontier and zero publications in flight;
+remote/service/output frontiers and due timer work still need their own proof.
+The earlier TaskJoins collector remains shutdown evidence only.
+
+The new Actor-work cases use actual sessions, command queues, WebSocket frames
+and real task joins. A controlled AsyncWrite gate supplies a causal blocked-write
+signal; it does not create a protocol message or replace the Actor. Each scenario
+uses one fixed five-second host deadline and no sleeps, retries or yield-count
+polling. Explicit state interleavings supplement these real-path cases for the
+acceptance-publication race and the maintenance-entry frontier: a command that
+returns during a pass remains uncovered until a later completed pass. The real
+image-replay case also requires that later pass. All pre-existing test bodies
+and bounds remain unchanged. This preparation does not migrate an original Voice
+scenario or add Supervisor/reconnect integration.
